From: SkillFishOS
Subject: [PATCH] drm/amd/pm: BC-250 - lower the declared minimum GFX clock to 350 MHz

Ariel's patch 03 routes the GFX clock through PMFW ForceGfxFreq and refuses
anything below CYAN_SKILLFISH_SCLK_MIN, which AMD declares as 1000 MHz:

    if (min < CYAN_SKILLFISH_SCLK_MIN || min > CYAN_SKILLFISH_SCLK_MAX)
            return -EINVAL;

Our cyan-skillfish-governor asks for 350 MHz at idle, the driver rejects it,
and the board sits at 1000 MHz doing nothing. Measured on the bc250-dev:
49 W idle with the Ariel series against 31 W on the stock kernel, for no gain
at all - 510 rounds of verified compute against 518, same zero errors, same
zero ring resets.

1000 is a declared floor, not a hardware one. The stock kernel runs this same
silicon at 350 MHz, and at 100, through the governor's direct SMU path.
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/pm/swsmu/smu11/cyan_skillfish_ppt.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/pm/swsmu/smu11/cyan_skillfish_ppt.c
@@ -52,7 +52,7 @@
 #undef pr_debug
 
 /* unit: MHz */
-#define CYAN_SKILLFISH_SCLK_MIN			1000
+#define CYAN_SKILLFISH_SCLK_MIN			350
 #define CYAN_SKILLFISH_SCLK_MAX			2500
 
 /* unit: mV */
